==German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ʃaʁf/|lang=de}} (''standard'')
* {{IPA|/ʃaːf/|lang=de}} (''widespread, esp. northern and central Germany'')
* {{audio|De-scharf.ogg|audio}}
* {{homophones|Schaf|lang=de}} (''not according to standard pronunciation'')

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|scarf|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*skarpaz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*(s)kerb(h)}}, from {{term/t|ine-pro|*(s)ker-||to cut}}. Compare Low German {{term|scharp|lang=nds}}, Dutch {{term|scherp|lang=nl}}, English {{term|sharp|lang=en}}, Danish {{term|skarp|lang=da}}.

